From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] deepseek-v4: native DSpark block and request-local verification widths

DeepSeek V4 DSpark drafts dspark_block_size (5) tokens in one parallel
pass, but n_predict was the MTP stage count (3), so num_speculative_tokens
had to be <=3 or a multiple of 3. Use the block size, as V4.1 does.

Extend the V4.1 verification-width hooks (spec_k, exact small-cohort
graphs, decode metadata, measured history policy) to V4, including its
resolved DeepseekV4ForConditionalGeneration architecture. The V4 history
policy uses a PP3 cost table measured on CMP 170HX and picks one shared
width per scheduled cohort, since mixed widths lose uniform FULL graphs.

Adds the opt-in VLLM_DSV41_OPT_PROFILE=v4-spec. Everything stays off
unless the profile or enable_adaptive_verification is set.
---
diff --git a/vllm/config/speculative.py b/vllm/config/speculative.py
index 331db79..9cc043d 100644
--- a/vllm/config/speculative.py
+++ b/vllm/config/speculative.py
@@ -1438,7 +1438,7 @@ class SpeculativeConfig:
                     draft_hf_config.architectures = [
                         "DSparkV41DraftModel" if is_v41 else "DSparkDraftModel"
                     ]
-                    if is_v41:
+                    if is_v41 or getattr(draft_hf_config, "dspark_block_size", None):
                         # hf_config_override set n_predict to the number of
                         # MTP stages (3), but one DSpark round drafts
                         # dspark_block_size tokens; num_speculative_tokens
@@ -1929,7 +1929,10 @@ class SpeculativeConfig:
         return bool(
             self.enable_adaptive_verification and self.use_dspark()
             and target is not None
-            and "DeepseekV41ForCausalLM" in target.architectures
+            # Same set as vllm.dsv41_opt_profile.VERIFICATION_WIDTH_ARCHS.
+            and not {"DeepseekV41ForCausalLM", "DeepseekV4ForCausalLM",
+                     "DeepseekV4ForConditionalGeneration"}.isdisjoint(
+                         target.architectures)
         )
 
     def uses_gpu_adaptive_verification(self) -> bool:
